<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">German South West Africa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">German <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/namibia">South West Africa</a> was a colony of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a> in present-day Namibia. German forces there carried out the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a> of the Herero and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nama-people">Nama peoples</a> in 1904–1908. It was lost to South African forces during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/german-south-west-africa.jpg" alt="German South West Africa" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Imperial Colonial Office of the German Empire Vector: David Liuzzo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Reichskolonialflagge.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
